Yao-Dong Li, Xiaoqun Wang, Gang Chen — arXiv:1608.07008v1 (2016)

## Generic model

The most general symmetry-allowed nearest-neighbor pseudospin model:

$$H_0 = \sum_{\langle rr'\rangle}\left[ J_x \tau_r^x \tau_{r'}^x + J_y \tau_r^y \tau_{r'}^y + J_z \tau_r^z \tau_{r'}^z + J_{yz}(\tau_r^y \tau_{r'}^z + \tau_r^z \tau_{r'}^y)\right]$$

where $\tau^x$ transforms as an **octupole** and $\tau^y,\tau^z$ as **dipoles** under the $D_{3d}$ space group.

## Reduced model

A rotation by angle $\theta$ about pseudospin-$x$ removes the $J_{yz}$ cross term:

$$H = \sum_{\langle rr'\rangle}\left[ J_x T_r^x T_{r'}^x + J_y T_r^y T_{r'}^y + J_z T_r^z T_{r'}^z\right] - h\sum_r\left[\cos\theta\, T_r^z + \sin\theta\, T_r^y\right]$$

with $T^x=\tau^x$, $T^y=\tau^z\sin\theta+\tau^y\cos\theta$, $T^z=\tau^z\cos\theta-\tau^y\sin\theta$.

## Ferro-octupolar (FO) state

On the $I_x$ surface ($J_x=-1$), $\langle T^x\rangle$ (octupole) orders ferromagnetically, breaking time-reversal symmetry. The mean-field transition is at

$$T_o = 1.5\,|J_x|.$$

Because the octupole $T^x$ does **not** couple linearly to the magnetic field, $\chi_{zz}$ shows **no divergence** at $T_o$.

## Octupolar-wave dispersion

$$\omega_k = \left[\Big(J_y\textstyle\sum_i \cos(k\cdot a_i)-3J_x\Big)\Big(J_z\textstyle\sum_i \cos(k\cdot a_i)-3J_x\Big)\right]^{1/2}$$

with $a_1=(1,0)$, $a_2=(-\tfrac12,\tfrac{\sqrt3}{2})$, $a_3=(-\tfrac12,-\tfrac{\sqrt3}{2})$. The mode is generically **gapped**.

## Mean-field 3-sublattice decoupling (AFO regimes)

$$H_{MF} = 3\sum_{r\in A}\sum_\mu J_\mu(m^\mu_B+m^\mu_C)T_r^\mu + (\text{B,C cyclic}) - h\sum_r[\cos\theta\,T_r^z+\sin\theta\,T_r^y]$$

with $m^\mu_\Lambda=\langle T_r^\mu\rangle$ solved self-consistently on sublattices $\Lambda=A,B,C$.
